# credscan-pinned-names.env — canonical pinned NAME list for credential-transcript-scan.sh
# OWNER: bun-desktop@mesh (instrument owner) · AUTHORITY: host GO 2026-09-02-003
# HOST PATH:      /mnt/system/base/skills/credscan/credscan-pinned-names.env
# CONTAINER PATH: /skills/credscan/credscan-pinned-names.env (same inode tree; ro-mounted in-container)
#
# WHAT THIS IS: every credential/env NAME the credscan instrument has ever hunted in
# ANY launch context — union of (s6 dir + /proc/self/environ + z-code-wrapper layers)
# across every "SELECTOR names:" line in /config/workspace/credential-transcript-scan.log
# 2026-08-04 → 2026-09-02, plus a live-layer check at build time (live layers added 0 new).
# NAMES ONLY — NEVER VALUES. A value that lives only in one launch's environ cannot be
# resolved outside it, so this pin buys OBSERVABILITY, not coverage: a name on this list
# that a launch cannot resolve is reported on that run's "SELECTOR pinned-names:" line as
#   NAME: ABSENT-IN-THIS-LAUNCH            (not in s6, environ, or wrapper this launch)
#   NAME(layer:len, present this launch but below qualify threshold — not huntable)
#
# DISCIPLINE: a name is ADDED here the first time it qualifies in any launch, and PRUNED
# only by a deliberate edit (rotation-out / retirement) recorded in the CHANGELOG below.
# Silence never prunes. Names below that are retired fleet-wide are kept DELIBERATELY —
# their ABSENT verdict is a visible coverage fact ("this launch cannot hunt Stripe at
# all"), not noise. When this file changes, the md5 on the selector line changes; valid
# cross-run comparison requires identical pin md5 AND both runs showing pin SOURCED.
#
# FORMAT: one NAME per line; '#' comments and blank lines ignored; no '=' values — a
# value in this file would be a credential at rest in a shared tree.

ADMIN_SEND_TOKEN
AGENTMAIL_API_KEY
